# RUN: llc -mtriple=aie2ps --start-before=postmisched -verify-machineinstrs \
# RUN:     -debug-only=sched-blocks -o /dev/null %s 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DBG
# REQUIRES: asserts
#
# Test sibling loop optimization: no merge due to non-matching prologues.
#
# Generated from conv2d_opt_outerloop_pipelining_out_mode_0.ll with:
#   llc -mtriple=aie2ps -O2 --aie-enable-outer-loop-pipelining
#       --aie-enable-sibling-loop-vreg-merge=false -stop-before=postmisched
#
# OLP structure:
#   bb.0-bb.4 (OuterPreheader) -> bb.5 (SteadyTop/Prologue)
#   -> bb.6 (SteadyInner) -> bb.7 (SteadyBottom/Epilogue/Latch)
#   -> bb.8 (PeeledIterTop) -> bb.9 (PeeledIterInner)
#   -> bb.10 (PeeledIterBottom)
#
# Without the AIESiblingLoopVRegMerger, the two prologues (SteadyTop
# and PeeledIterTop) use different physical registers for the same
# logical operations. This causes countMatchingLeadingBundles to
# return 0 because the leading bundles differ in register operands.
#
# Result: The optimizer detects the OLP structure but finds no matching
# bundles between the two prologues and bails out immediately.
#
# Verify the optimizer finds no matching bundles.
# DBG: optimizeSiblingLoops: Processing outer loop latch
# DBG: No matching bundles between prologues
